Actually, wait. An empty label is not valid in DNS. But the code doesn't check for it. If the name is `\x00\x00`, the first byte is 0 (root label), so the loop terminates immediately. The second byte is not processed. This is correct.

But what if the name is `\x01a\x00\x00`? The first label is 'a', then the root label terminates the name. The second root label is not processed. This is correct.

